    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\nvoid body_force(float *px, float *py, float *pz,\\n                float *vx, float *vy, float *vz,\\n                float dt, int n) {\\n  #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static, 1)\\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n    float xi = px[i];\\n    float yi = py[i];\\n    float zi = pz[i];\\n    float fx = 0.0f;\\n    float fy = 0.0f;\\n    float fz = 0.0f;\\n\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n      float dx = px[j] - xi;\\n      float dy = py[j] - yi;\\n      float dz = pz[j] - zi;\\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n      float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n    }\\n\\n    vx[i] += dt*fx;\\n    vy[i] += dt*fy;\\n    vz[i] += dt*fz;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n  float *px = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n  float *py = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n  float *pz = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n  float *vx = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n  float *vy = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n  float *vz = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n    px[i] = bodies[i].x;\\n    py[i] = bodies[i].y;\\n    pz[i] = bodies[i].z;\\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\\n  }\\n\\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\\n    body_force(px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz, DT, nbodies);\\n\\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n      px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\\n      py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\\n      pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n    bodies[i].x = px[i];\\n    bodies[i].y = py[i];\\n    bodies[i].z = pz[i];\\n    bodies[i].vx = vx[i];\\n    bodies[i].vy = vy[i];\\n    bodies[i].vz = vz[i];\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(px); free(py); free(pz);\\n  free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\\n  free(bodies);\\n\\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Converting the body data from an array-of-structs to a structure-of-arrays layout gives three sequential float streams (x, y, z) for the inner j-loop instead of interleaved struct fields, improving cache line utilization. Parallelizing the i-loop with OpenMP schedule(static,1) distributes independent per-body force accumulations round-robin across 4 cores, balancing load and keeping all threads reading similar ranges of the position arrays concurrently to maximize shared-cache reuse, while preserving exact j-order summation for bit-identical output.\",\n  \"notes\": \"The SoA conversion is done once before the iteration loop and reversed only at output; arithmetic order per body is unchanged. OpenMP static(1) on the force l